      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yes please, love the immersion of turning nametags off but when I want to check one new arrival's name sometimes I have to then fill my entire screen with nametags (and then sometimes if it's really busy there's so many I can't even read the tag, or select them either because good luck finding the right capsule in that mess lmao)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-07-07T00:45:05.596Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hiding nametags reduces visual clutter quite a lot, however there is a drastic downside to using this feature: you have no idea who anyone is unless you repeatedly open the menu when new people show up.\n\nAdd a third option for nametags, \"Temporary\", which will show a person's nametag the first time they are rendered to you in an instance for 5-10 seconds, and then fade it away and hide it from then on in that instance. To avoid issues of this occurring when the person is too far away, the trigger distance for this should be reasonably close, let's say 7-10 meters.\n\nOptionally, when a person changes their avatar after already having been rendered, their nametag should be queued to be temporarily shown again when you load the avatar they changed into, to avoid confusion as to who this seemingly new person is (if they changed while not visible to you).",
